# Standard profile: Ctrl+` opens the scratch terminal strip; Ctrl+P with
# the strip focused opens b.txt in the EDITOR AREA (beside a.txt), never
# as a tab of the strip — the strip hosts terminals only, as VS Code's
# terminal panel does. Ctrl+` twice (focus, hide) then leaves one leaf
# with b.txt active and a.txt a background tab: no stray split.
# (hunt/findings-2026-09-23/std-scratch-strip-swallows-opened-files.md)
write a.txt "AAA-top\n"
write b.txt "BBB-picked\n"
open a.txt
key ctrl+`
wait 1500
expect status contains "scratch"
key ctrl+p
type b.txt
key enter
expect screen contains "BBB-picked"
# Hide the strip: the first Ctrl+` refocuses the terminal tab, the second hides it.
key ctrl+`
wait 300
key ctrl+`
wait 300
expect screen contains "BBB-picked"
expect screen lacks "AAA-top"
